Subject: [PATCH] [M159] Fix for potential UAF in PermissionRequestManager
 selectors logic

Original change's description:
> Fix for potential UAF in PermissionRequestManager selectors logic
>
> When PermissionRequestManager::DequeueRequestIfNeeded() resolves
> selectors synchronously, OnPermissionUiSelectorDone() can call
> ShowPrompt(), which drops fullscreen via ForSecurityDropFullscreen(). If
> the WebContents is destroyed during fullscreen exit, ShowPrompt() safely
> early-returns, but returns void to its caller.
>
> When execution unwinds back to DequeueRequestIfNeeded(), the selector
> loop attempts to evaluate permission_ui_selectors_.size() on freed
> memory, causing a Heap-Use-After-Free under AddressSanitizer.
>
> This CL guards the selector loop in DequeueRequestIfNeeded() with a
> WeakPtr check after synchronous selector callbacks to ensure the manager
> has not been destroyed before continuing the loop.
>
> A regression test is added under #if defined(ADDRESS_SANITIZER) using a
> mock selector to deterministically simulate synchronous destruction
> without relying on platform-specific fullscreen window manager
> behaviors.
>
